 mean number of June–August days per season at or above 26.0 °C, and where the reference day ranks inside the pooled June–August distribution.","interpretation_boundary":"This daily-maximum WBGT archive is from the same UrbClim model family and 100 m grid as the committed ranking raster, but it reports °C daily maxima while that raster is a normalized 0–100 indicator for a 24-hour mean scenario. It can test sensitivity to heat-period choice, but its values are not interchangeable with the raster and it does not replace the ranking input. The 2008–2017 window cannot show future climate change.","grid":{"note":"Nearest 100 m cell at each tree point; the sampled trees fall into 39 distinct cells.","rows":301,"columns":301,"step_metres":100.0},"related_publication":"Souverijns et al. 2026, Data in Brief 65, 112497, doi 10.1016/j.dib.2026.112497","archive_urls":["https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2008.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2009.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2010.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2011.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2012.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2013.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2014.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2015.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2016.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2017.nc"],"source_page":"https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/","crs":"EPSG:3035","archive_base_url":"https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels","window":{"seasons":10,"end_year":2017,"start_year":2008,"years":[2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017],"months":["06","07","08"]},"source":"VITO UrbClim daily 100 m WBGT archive for Brussels","region_summary":{"hot_days_per_season_min":2.8,"reference_date_wbgt_min_c":26.13,"trees":100,"reference_percentile_max":97.6,"seasonal_mean_wbgt_spread_c":1.41,"seasonal_mean_wbgt_max_c":20.51,"distinct_cells":39,"reference_percentile_min":96.7,"reference_percentile_mean":97.3,"reference_date_wbgt_max_c":27.52,"hot_days_per_season_max":7.0,"seasonal_mean_wbgt_min_c":19.1,"reference_date_wbgt_spread_c":1.39},"licence_review":{"related_records":[{"name":"Copernicus Climate Data Store: Climate variables for cities in Europe from 2008 to 2017","covers":"Hourly air temperature, specific humidity, relative humidity and wind speed for 100 European cities including Brussels, 2008–2017; contains no WBGT","status":"Deprecated on the CDS on 2024-05-10; VITO now serves the historical 2008–2017 archive itself","licence":"CC-BY-4.0","applies_to_this_archive":false,"catalogue_record":"https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/api/catalogue/v1/collections/sis-urban-climate-cities"},{"name":"Souverijns et al. (2026) decadal climate and heat-stress indicator set","covers":"Decadal 2010–2100 indicators (GeoTIFF and NetCDF) for 142 cities, not the daily 2008–2017 files","status":"Separate record","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.13361538","licence":"CC BY 4.0","applies_to_this_archive":false}],"status":"unresolved","detail":"The archive page asks users to cite both De Ridder et al. (2015) and Souverijns et al. (2026), but states no licence or redistribution terms, and the annual NetCDF files carry no licence attribute: their global attributes are only crs, title, institution (VITO), creator and source (UrbClim). Two related records do not transfer their terms to this archive. The Souverijns et al. (2026) decadal 2010–2100 indicator set is CC BY 4.0, and the Copernicus Climate Data Store record 'Climate variables for cities in Europe from 2008 to 2017' (sis-urban-climate-cities, deprecated 2024-05-10) is CC-BY-4.0 with Brussels among its 100 cities and 2008–2017 coverage — but that record contains hourly air temperature, specific humidity, relative humidity and wind speed, and no WBGT, while this archive adds WBGT, daily aggregation and further cities. Confirm the daily-file and derived-value terms with VITO (urbclim@vito.be) before external reuse."},"value_semantics":"UrbClim 2 m Wet Bulb Globe Temperature, degrees Celsius, daily maximum, on a 100 m grid in EPSG:3035; computed with the Liljegren et al. (2008) method following ISO 7243","period_sensitivity":{"note":"Cross-screen overlaps compare each VITO heat-only alternative with the current balanced raster-plus-proximity screen; they are descriptive and combine differences in WBGT output semantics, heat period and scoring. The three reference-day comparisons relate aggregations of the same VITO daily-maximum series to the same reference day, so they describe temporal sensitivity within the archive and are the comparable set; all three answer the heat-period question at the same resolution and source. None of these comparisons selects a ranking.","balanced_top_ten_ids":["vbx_56561","vbx_56558","vbx_56544","vbx_56550","vbx_56554","vbx_56557","vbx_56567","vbx_56573","vbx_56571","vbx_56818"],"top_ten_overlap":{"seasonal_mean_vs_balanced":0,"hot_days_vs_balanced":0,"seasonal_p90_vs_balanced":0,"seasonal_mean_vs_reference_day":7,"reference_day_vs_balanced":3,"seasonal_p90_vs_reference_day":7,"hot_days_vs_reference_day":7}},"reference_date":"2016-08-24"}
